Z||000001||Old Lar||10-20-2000||07:36 AM||||Depends on how fast you can shift the manual transmission.  Usually automatics don't let you go to redline unless you do manual shifting of the automatic.  The 5 speed has more gears to go through than the 3 speed automatic, but that is sort of irrelevent since 4th and 5th are overdrives.<BR>I can reach ~60 in 2nd, ~90 in 3rd with the 5 speed.  The rev limiter cuts in at about 60 in 2nd.  With the manual you can lunch at higher rpms.   Skill come into play.||||reg||1
Z||000002||Xtreme Fiero's||10-20-2000||08:41 AM||||the 4.10 4 speed will get you down the 1/4 mile faster than any other. bu top speed would be limited to arout 100-110 mph. while my friends 88 GT and anoter friends 87 GT where both automatics and a good race for my 84 SE until around 100-110 when they just kept going faster but they both toped out at 120 & 125 respectfull.<P>PS the 87 GT has 75k miles (chick driver) and the 88 GT 125k+ and a moron driveing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||1
